Translate macOS direct touches into GPUI touches: the decisions, on plain values.

What: a new `gpui_macos` module, `window/touch.rs`, with no AppKit calls; patch 0026 wires it to AppKit.
- `PHASES`: `NSTouchPhase` bit → `TouchPhase` (Began → Started, Moved, Ended, Cancelled; stationary touches carry
  nothing new and have no row). `CHANGED` and `TOUCHING` are the phase masks the recognizer reads touches by.
- `TouchIds<K>`: GPUI's ids for the live touches, keyed by `NSTouch.identity` (generic, so tested without AppKit),
  with each touch's last position. `track` gives a begin the next `TouchId` (from 0, wrapping) and drops a move or
  end with no live begin; a begin of an identity still live cancels that stale touch where it was, then starts its
  own, the rule gpui_windows (0021) and gpui_linux's Wayland (0022) follow. `cancel_all` cancels every live touch
  where it last was (AppKit reset the recognizer).
- `RecognizerState` (NSGestureRecognizer.h's states, decoded from AppKit's `NSInteger` by `from_raw`) and
  `next_state(state, Left)`, one row per (state, what the event left: fingers `Touching`, the last `Lifted` or
  `Cancelled`): the recognizer claims a sequence from its first touch (`Began`, then `Changed`) and finishes
  `Ended` or `Cancelled` when no finger is down; a sequence that ends within its first event fails; nothing moves
  on from `Ended`, `Cancelled` or `Failed`, which AppKit resets itself (the legal transitions only).
- `TouchQueue`: touches on their way to GPUI's input callback; while the callback is busy (AppKit re-enters the
  run loop inside it) an end or cancel waits and a start or move is dropped, so no touch stays open.
- `TOUCH_COPIES` / `is_touch_copy`: the mouse, scroll and magnify events AppKit makes from direct touches in an app
  without `NSIsTouchNative`, dropped while the recognizer holds touches (mouse events by `subtype ==
  NSEventSubtypeTouch`; scroll and magnify carry no subtype, so any mid-touch), as 0021 drops `MI_WP_SIGNATURE`
  copies and 0023 `XIPointerEmulated` ones.
Table tests: `touch_phases`, `recognizer_states`, `touch_ids`, `touch_queue`, `touch_copies` (run on a Mac:
`cargo test -p parallax-gpui-macos --features test-support --lib touch`). Nothing calls the module until 0026.

Why: macOS 27 delivers direct touches (a touchscreen Mac, an iPad by Sidecar) to gesture recognizers only, and
GPUI's macOS backend had none; its window and view are private, so neither a Parallax crate nor an extension trait
can add this. Kept apart from the AppKit glue (0026) so each patch has one concern (AGENTS.md patch rule 4). cfg:
the crate's own (macOS).

Upstream PR: not filed yet.

